  "details": "A simple optimized component for turning unity transform data into parameters in the animator. Much like how a physbone component or a contact component can send data into the animator, this component would send a variation of transform data without expensive optimized workarounds.\n\nThis would be useful for a variety of complex rigs and avatar systems. For example activating blendshapes to solve clipping when limbs are at extreme angles, or to have features enable when your hands are close together.  \n\nAt the moment, most of this can be solved with large and complex contact point systems that clutters the workflow and feels like a hack. A more optimized toolset would enable avatar creators to work more efficiently, creature more optimized assets, and expand avatar immersion with ideas yet to come.\n\nThis component, or collection of components, would be able to track:\n\n  * The angle of a bone in relation to another bone, or its parent if no other bone is assigned.\n\n  * The rotation (Euler angles) of a bone in relation to the world or an assigned bone.\n\n  * The distance between two bones.\n\n  * The current coordinates (vector3) of the bone in relation to the world or an assigned bone.\n\nAll of this would be done locally on the avatar and each remote instance of it, so no need to sync the data.",
